# Build-gate self-test fixtures. The gates prove they can fail by generating a
# tree with a planted violation, running against it, and deleting it. A fixture
# left behind by an interrupted run must never be committed — it contains
# deliberate §1.8 rule-2 violations and bare constants that would mislead a
# reader into thinking real defects had been checked in.
/tests/gates/.fixtures/
